module

public import MathlibExt.Analysis.VonNeumannAlgebra.IsometryConjugation
public import MathlibExt.Analysis.VonNeumannAlgebra.NormalAction.DoubleCrossedProductTensor
public import MathlibExt.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Group.HaarL2.RadonProduct.HFirst

/-!
# Double crossed-product operators on a Borel Radon model

For a Hausdorff locally compact group with regular Haar measure `μ`, and regular Haar measure
`ν` on its Borel character group, use the normal dual action to form the double tensor crossed
product `C₂`. The unitary `U` from its nested Hilbert tensor to `L_R=Lp H 2 (radonProd μ ν)`
transports its operators by `A ↦ U A U⁻¹`.

The transported first-coefficient and second-group images generate a von Neumann algebra on
`L_R`. Their canonical coefficient and unitary maps retain these conjugation values. The measure
is on the Borel topological product `G×PontryaginDual G`, without a countability assumption or
normalized Fourier transform.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

open MeasureTheory UniformSpace
open scoped TensorProduct CStarAlgebra

namespace VonNeumannAlgebra.NormalAction

noncomputable section

universe uG uH

variable {G : Type uG} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G]
  [T2Space G] [LocallyCompactSpace G] [MeasurableSpace G] [BorelSpace G]
variable {H : Type uH} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]
variable {M : VonNeumannAlgebra H}
variable (μ : Measure G) [μ.IsHaarMeasure] [μ.Regular]
variable [MeasurableSpace (PontryaginDual G)] [BorelSpace (PontryaginDual G)]
variable (ν : Measure (PontryaginDual G)) [ν.IsHaarMeasure] [ν.Regular]

/-- **Borel structure on the group and character-group product.** For a group `G` with
topology, the measurable structure on `G×PontryaginDual G` is the Borel structure of its
product topology. -/
local instance instDoubleRadonProductMeasurableSpace :
    MeasurableSpace (G × PontryaginDual G) := borel (G × PontryaginDual G)
local instance instDoubleRadonProductBorelSpace : BorelSpace (G × PontryaginDual G) := ⟨rfl⟩

/-- **Normal spatial map from the double tensor algebra to Radon L².** Let `G` be a locally
compact topological group with its Borel structure and regular Haar measure `μ`, `H` a
complete complex Hilbert space, and `α` a normal action on `M⊆B(H)` with norm-continuous
inverse predual orbits. Put `T=Completion(H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ)` and let `U₀ : T ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] Lp H 2
μ` send `ξ⊗f` to the L² class represented μ-almost everywhere by `s ↦ f(s) • ξ`. For `P_x
ξ =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ α_(s⁻¹)(x)ξ(s))`, put `Q_x=U₀⁻¹P_xU₀`. Let `C₁` be generated by `Q_x` and
`V_g=I_H⊗λ_g`, where `λ_g f =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ f(g⁻¹s))`. Write `Γ=PontryaginDual G`, with its
Borel measurable structure, and let `ν` be a regular Haar measure on `Γ`. Let `β` be the
normal character action on `C₁`, and set `C₂=C₁⋊_β Γ` on `D=Completion(T ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν)`.
Assume also that `G` is Hausdorff. Let `U : D ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] L_R` be the tensor-to-Radon unitary,
where `L_R=Lp H 2 (radonProd μ ν)` on the Borel topological product `G×Γ`. Write `j₂ : C₁
→ C₂` for the second regular coefficient map. `doubleRadonSpatialNormalHom μ ν α : C₂ →
B(L_R)` is the normal unital star homomorphism `A ↦ U A U⁻¹`.

Here `=ᵐ[μ]` denotes equality of measurable representatives μ-almost everywhere, not point
evaluation of an L² class. Operator identities are equalities of bounded operators. The
product-space L² class uses the stated measure `radonProd μ ν`. -/
def doubleRadonSpatialNormalHom (α : NormalAction G M) :
    NormalStarAlgHom (doubleCrossedProductTensor μ ν α)
      (⊤ : VonNeumannAlgebra (Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν))) :=
  isometryConjugationNormalHom (HaarL2.radonProductHFirstTensorUnitary (H := H) μ ν)
    (doubleCrossedProductTensor μ ν α)

/-- **Operator value of double Radon spatial conjugation.** Let `G` be a locally compact
topological group with its Borel structure and regular Haar measure `μ`, `H` a complete
complex Hilbert space, and `α` a normal action on `M⊆B(H)` with norm-continuous inverse
predual orbits. Put `T=Completion(H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ)` and let `U₀ : T ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] Lp H 2 μ` send
`ξ⊗f` to the L² class represented μ-almost everywhere by `s ↦ f(s) • ξ`. For `P_x ξ =ᵐ[μ]
(s ↦ α_(s⁻¹)(x)ξ(s))`, put `Q_x=U₀⁻¹P_xU₀`. Let `C₁` be generated by `Q_x` and
`V_g=I_H⊗λ_g`, where `λ_g f =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ f(g⁻¹s))`. Write `Γ=PontryaginDual G`, with its
Borel measurable structure, and let `ν` be a regular Haar measure on `Γ`. Let `β` be the
normal character action on `C₁`, and set `C₂=C₁⋊_β Γ` on `D=Completion(T ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν)`.
Assume also that `G` is Hausdorff. Let `U : D ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] L_R` be the tensor-to-Radon unitary,
where `L_R=Lp H 2 (radonProd μ ν)` on the Borel topological product `G×Γ`. Write `j₂ : C₁
→ C₂` for the second regular coefficient map. for `A∈C₂`, the bounded operator underlying
`doubleRadonSpatialNormalHom μ ν α A` is `U A U⁻¹`.

Here `=ᵐ[μ]` denotes equality of measurable representatives μ-almost everywhere, not point
evaluation of an L² class. Operator identities are equalities of bounded operators. The
product-space L² class uses the stated measure `radonProd μ ν`. -/
theorem doubleRadonSpatialNormalHom_coe (α : NormalAction G M)
    (x : doubleCrossedProductTensor μ ν α) :
    (doubleRadonSpatialNormalHom μ ν α x :
      Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν) →L[ℂ] Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν)) =
      (HaarL2.radonProductHFirstTensorUnitary (H := H) μ ν).conjStarAlgEquiv
        (x : Completion (Completion (H ⊗[ℂ] (Lp ℂ 2 μ)) ⊗[ℂ] (Lp ℂ 2 ν)) →L[ℂ]
          Completion (Completion (H ⊗[ℂ] (Lp ℂ 2 μ)) ⊗[ℂ] (Lp ℂ 2 ν))) := rfl

/-- **Normal first-algebra coefficient on the double Radon model.** Let `G` be a locally
compact topological group with its Borel structure and regular Haar measure `μ`, `H` a
complete complex Hilbert space, and `α` a normal action on `M⊆B(H)` with norm-continuous
inverse predual orbits. Put `T=Completion(H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ)` and let `U₀ : T ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] Lp H 2
μ` send `ξ⊗f` to the L² class represented μ-almost everywhere by `s ↦ f(s) • ξ`. For `P_x
ξ =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ α_(s⁻¹)(x)ξ(s))`, put `Q_x=U₀⁻¹P_xU₀`. Let `C₁` be generated by `Q_x` and
`V_g=I_H⊗λ_g`, where `λ_g f =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ f(g⁻¹s))`. Write `Γ=PontryaginDual G`, with its
Borel measurable structure, and let `ν` be a regular Haar measure on `Γ`. Let `β` be the
normal character action on `C₁`, and set `C₂=C₁⋊_β Γ` on `D=Completion(T ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν)`.
Assume also that `G` is Hausdorff. Let `U : D ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] L_R` be the tensor-to-Radon unitary,
where `L_R=Lp H 2 (radonProd μ ν)` on the Borel topological product `G×Γ`. Write `j₂ : C₁
→ C₂` for the second regular coefficient map. `doubleRadonFirstCoefficientNormalHom μ ν α
: C₁ → B(L_R)` is `x ↦ U j₂(x) U⁻¹`.

Here `=ᵐ[μ]` denotes equality of measurable representatives μ-almost everywhere, not point
evaluation of an L² class. Operator identities are equalities of bounded operators. The
product-space L² class uses the stated measure `radonProd μ ν`. -/
def doubleRadonFirstCoefficientNormalHom (α : NormalAction G M) :
    NormalStarAlgHom (crossedProductTensor μ α)
      (⊤ : VonNeumannAlgebra (Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν))) :=
  (doubleRadonSpatialNormalHom μ ν α).comp
    (crossedProductTensorCoefficientNormalHom ν (tensorCharacterNormalAction μ α))

/-- **Conjugated first-algebra coefficient operator.** Let `G` be a locally compact
topological group with its Borel structure and regular Haar measure `μ`, `H` a complete
complex Hilbert space, and `α` a normal action on `M⊆B(H)` with norm-continuous inverse
predual orbits. Put `T=Completion(H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ)` and let `U₀ : T ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] Lp H 2 μ` send
`ξ⊗f` to the L² class represented μ-almost everywhere by `s ↦ f(s) • ξ`. For `P_x ξ =ᵐ[μ]
(s ↦ α_(s⁻¹)(x)ξ(s))`, put `Q_x=U₀⁻¹P_xU₀`. Let `C₁` be generated by `Q_x` and
`V_g=I_H⊗λ_g`, where `λ_g f =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ f(g⁻¹s))`. Write `Γ=PontryaginDual G`, with its
Borel measurable structure, and let `ν` be a regular Haar measure on `Γ`. Let `β` be the
normal character action on `C₁`, and set `C₂=C₁⋊_β Γ` on `D=Completion(T ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν)`.
Assume also that `G` is Hausdorff. Let `U : D ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] L_R` be the tensor-to-Radon unitary,
where `L_R=Lp H 2 (radonProd μ ν)` on the Borel topological product `G×Γ`. Write `j₂ : C₁
→ C₂` for the second regular coefficient map. for `x∈C₁`, the operator of the first normal
coefficient is `U Q₂(x) U⁻¹`, where `Q₂(x)=regularCoefficientTensor ν β x` is the second
tensor coefficient.

Here `=ᵐ[μ]` denotes equality of measurable representatives μ-almost everywhere, not point
evaluation of an L² class. Operator identities are equalities of bounded operators. The
product-space L² class uses the stated measure `radonProd μ ν`. -/
theorem doubleRadonFirstCoefficientNormalHom_coe (α : NormalAction G M)
    (x : crossedProductTensor μ α) :
    (doubleRadonFirstCoefficientNormalHom μ ν α x :
      Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν) →L[ℂ] Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν)) =
      (HaarL2.radonProductHFirstTensorUnitary (H := H) μ ν).conjStarAlgEquiv
        (regularCoefficientTensor ν (tensorCharacterNormalAction μ α) x) := by
  let z : doubleCrossedProductTensor μ ν α :=
    crossedProductTensorCoefficientNormalHom ν (tensorCharacterNormalAction μ α) x
  have hx : (z : Completion (Completion (H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ) ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν) →L[ℂ]
      Completion (Completion (H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ) ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν)) =
        regularCoefficientTensor ν (tensorCharacterNormalAction μ α) x :=
    crossedProductTensorCoefficientNormalHom_coe ν (tensorCharacterNormalAction μ α) x
  calc
    _ = (doubleRadonSpatialNormalHom μ ν α z :
        Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν) →L[ℂ] Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν)) := rfl
    _ = (HaarL2.radonProductHFirstTensorUnitary (H := H) μ ν).conjStarAlgEquiv
        (z : Completion (Completion (H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ) ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν) →L[ℂ]
          Completion (Completion (H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ) ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν)) :=
      doubleRadonSpatialNormalHom_coe μ ν α z
    _ = _ := by
      apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext
      intro ξ
      simp only [LinearIsometryEquiv.conjStarAlgEquiv_apply_apply]
      exact congrArg
        (fun η : Completion (Completion (H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ) ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν) =>
          HaarL2.radonProductHFirstTensorUnitary (H := H) μ ν η)
        (congrArg
          (fun T : Completion (Completion (H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ) ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν) →L[ℂ]
            Completion (Completion (H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ) ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν) =>
              T ((HaarL2.radonProductHFirstTensorUnitary (H := H) μ ν).symm ξ)) hx)

/-- **Vector value of the first double Radon coefficient.** Let `G` be a locally compact
topological group with its Borel structure and regular Haar measure `μ`, `H` a complete
complex Hilbert space, and `α` a normal action on `M⊆B(H)` with norm-continuous inverse
predual orbits. Put `T=Completion(H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ)` and let `U₀ : T ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] Lp H 2 μ` send
`ξ⊗f` to the L² class represented μ-almost everywhere by `s ↦ f(s) • ξ`. For `P_x ξ =ᵐ[μ]
(s ↦ α_(s⁻¹)(x)ξ(s))`, put `Q_x=U₀⁻¹P_xU₀`. Let `C₁` be generated by `Q_x` and
`V_g=I_H⊗λ_g`, where `λ_g f =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ f(g⁻¹s))`. Write `Γ=PontryaginDual G`, with its
Borel measurable structure, and let `ν` be a regular Haar measure on `Γ`. Let `β` be the
normal character action on `C₁`, and set `C₂=C₁⋊_β Γ` on `D=Completion(T ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν)`.
Assume also that `G` is Hausdorff. Let `U : D ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] L_R` be the tensor-to-Radon unitary,
where `L_R=Lp H 2 (radonProd μ ν)` on the Borel topological product `G×Γ`. Write `j₂ : C₁
→ C₂` for the second regular coefficient map. for `x∈C₁`, `ξ∈L_R`, the first coefficient
sends `ξ` to `U(Q₂(x)(U⁻¹ξ))`, where `Q₂=regularCoefficientTensor ν β`.

Here `=ᵐ[μ]` denotes equality of measurable representatives μ-almost everywhere, not point
evaluation of an L² class. Operator identities are equalities of bounded operators. The
product-space L² class uses the stated measure `radonProd μ ν`. -/
theorem doubleRadonFirstCoefficientNormalHom_apply (α : NormalAction G M)
    (x : crossedProductTensor μ α) (ξ : Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν)) :
    (doubleRadonFirstCoefficientNormalHom μ ν α x :
      Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν) →L[ℂ] Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν)) ξ =
      HaarL2.radonProductHFirstTensorUnitary (H := H) μ ν
        (regularCoefficientTensor ν (tensorCharacterNormalAction μ α) x
          ((HaarL2.radonProductHFirstTensorUnitary (H := H) μ ν).symm ξ)) := by
  calc
    _ = ((HaarL2.radonProductHFirstTensorUnitary (H := H) μ ν).conjStarAlgEquiv
        (regularCoefficientTensor ν (tensorCharacterNormalAction μ α) x)) ξ :=
      congrArg
        (fun T : Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν) →L[ℂ] Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν) => T ξ)
        (doubleRadonFirstCoefficientNormalHom_coe μ ν α x)
    _ = _ := rfl

/-- **Composed normal coefficient into the double tensor algebra.** Let `G` be a locally
compact topological group with its Borel structure and regular Haar measure `μ`, `H` a
complete complex Hilbert space, and `α` a normal action on `M⊆B(H)` with norm-continuous
inverse predual orbits. Put `T=Completion(H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ)` and let `U₀ : T ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] Lp H 2
μ` send `ξ⊗f` to the L² class represented μ-almost everywhere by `s ↦ f(s) • ξ`. For `P_x
ξ =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ α_(s⁻¹)(x)ξ(s))`, put `Q_x=U₀⁻¹P_xU₀`. Let `C₁` be generated by `Q_x` and
`V_g=I_H⊗λ_g`, where `λ_g f =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ f(g⁻¹s))`. Write `Γ=PontryaginDual G`, with its
Borel measurable structure, and let `ν` be a regular Haar measure on `Γ`. Let `β` be the
normal character action on `C₁`, and set `C₂=C₁⋊_β Γ` on `D=Completion(T ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν)`.
Assume also that `G` is Hausdorff. Let `U : D ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] L_R` be the tensor-to-Radon unitary,
where `L_R=Lp H 2 (radonProd μ ν)` on the Borel topological product `G×Γ`. Write `j₂ : C₁
→ C₂` for the second regular coefficient map. `doubleTensorCoefficientNormalHom μ ν α : M
→ C₂` is `j₂∘j₁`, where `j₁ : M → C₁` is the first tensor coefficient inclusion.

Here `=ᵐ[μ]` denotes equality of measurable representatives μ-almost everywhere, not point
evaluation of an L² class. Operator identities are equalities of bounded operators. The
product-space L² class uses the stated measure `radonProd μ ν`. -/
def doubleTensorCoefficientNormalHom (α : NormalAction G M) :
    NormalStarAlgHom M (doubleCrossedProductTensor μ ν α) :=
  (crossedProductTensorCoefficientNormalHom ν (tensorCharacterNormalAction μ α)).comp
    (crossedProductTensorCoefficientNormalHom μ α)

/-- **Normal source coefficient into double Radon operators.** Let `G` be a locally compact
topological group with its Borel structure and regular Haar measure `μ`, `H` a complete
complex Hilbert space, and `α` a normal action on `M⊆B(H)` with norm-continuous inverse
predual orbits. Put `T=Completion(H ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 μ)` and let `U₀ : T ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] Lp H 2 μ` send
`ξ⊗f` to the L² class represented μ-almost everywhere by `s ↦ f(s) • ξ`. For `P_x ξ =ᵐ[μ]
(s ↦ α_(s⁻¹)(x)ξ(s))`, put `Q_x=U₀⁻¹P_xU₀`. Let `C₁` be generated by `Q_x` and
`V_g=I_H⊗λ_g`, where `λ_g f =ᵐ[μ] (s ↦ f(g⁻¹s))`. Write `Γ=PontryaginDual G`, with its
Borel measurable structure, and let `ν` be a regular Haar measure on `Γ`. Let `β` be the
normal character action on `C₁`, and set `C₂=C₁⋊_β Γ` on `D=Completion(T ⊗[ℂ] Lp ℂ 2 ν)`.
Assume also that `G` is Hausdorff. Let `U : D ≃ₗᵢ[ℂ] L_R` be the tensor-to-Radon unitary,
where `L_R=Lp H 2 (radonProd μ ν)` on the Borel topological product `G×Γ`. Write `j₂ : C₁
→ C₂` for the second regular coefficient map. `doubleRadonCoefficientNormalHom μ ν α : M →
B(L_R)` sends `x` to `U j₂(j₁(x)) U⁻¹`.

Here `=ᵐ[μ]` denotes equality of measurable representatives μ-almost everywhere, not point
evaluation of an L² class. Operator identities are equalities of bounded operators. The
product-space L² class uses the stated measure `radonProd μ ν`. -/
def doubleRadonCoefficientNormalHom (α : NormalAction G M) :
    NormalStarAlgHom M (⊤ : VonNeumannAlgebra (Lp H 2 (Measure.radonProd μ ν))) :=
  (doubleRadonSpatialNormalHom μ ν α).comp (doubleTensorCoefficientNormalHom μ ν α)

